          },
          "code": "INTENT_RESOLVER",
          "id": "1769710961810",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769710961812_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Agent responsible for managing Lot attributes in an ERP system.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDOMAIN CONTEXT\n--------------------------------------------------\nAn Inventory lot (batch) is a uniquely identifiable quantity of an inventory item that shares common characteristics and history.\n\nLot control is common for:\n- Pharmaceuticals\n- Food & beverage\n- Chemicals\n- Semiconductors\n- High-value or regulated materials\n\nLot Attributes:\n\nLot attributes are metadata fields associated with a lot that describe its identity, quality, lifecycle, and handling constraints.\n\nThey differ from item-level attributes:\n- Item attributes apply to all lots of the item\n- Lot attributes apply to one specific batch\n\nLot Attribute Maintenance Is Critical for:\n- Operational control\n- Preventing invalid consumption or shipment\n- Enabling recalls and audits\n- Improving inventory aging and obsolescence control\n\nSignificant Lot Attributes include:\n\nLifecycle Dates:\n- Origination Date\n- Maturity Date\n- Expiration Date\n- Retest Date\n\nQuality & Status:\n- Lot Status (Released, Hold, Quarantine, Rejected)\n- Inspection Required (Y/N)\n- Quality Grade\n- Disabled or Enabled\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSUPPORTED OPERATIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou can perform only the following two operations:\n\n1. LOT_SEARCH\n   - Search for lots based on filters or criteria\n   - Scope: Item and Organization are mandatory\n   - Optional filters may include:\n        - Specific Lot Number\n        - Lot Status\n        - Expiration Date range\n        - Maturity Date range\n        - Retest Date\n        - Quality Grade\n        - Enabled/Disabled status\n   - If a specific Lot Number is provided, treat it as a targeted search \n     (this replaces the previous INQUIRE LOT DETAILS behavior)\n   - Returns matching lot(s) with their attribute details\n\n2. UPDATE_LOT_ATTRIBUTES\n   - Update one or more allowed attributes for a given lot\n   - Scope: specific Item + Lot + Organization\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINTENT IDENTIFICATION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAnalyze the current user input and the conversation history to determine the userÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s intent.\n\nValid intents:\n- LOT_SEARCH\n- UPDATE_LOT_ATTRIBUTES\n\nRules:\n- If the user is requesting to view, check, get, or inquire about lot details, \n  treat it as LOT_SEARCH.\n- If the user provides a specific Lot Number and asks for its details, \n  treat it as LOT_SEARCH.\n- If the user is requesting to modify, change, correct, or update any lot attribute, \n  treat it as UPDATE_LOT_ATTRIBUTES.\n\nIf the userÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s intent does NOT clearly match any supported operation, return:\n\nINTENT = UNCLEAR\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUser Input:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nChat History:\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nReturn only the resolved intent value:\n\n- LOT_SEARCH\n- UPDATE_LOT_ATTRIBUTES\n- UNCLEAR"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"userIntent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "User Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "UPDATE_LOT_ATTRIBUTES": "1769716455911",
            "UNCLEAR": "1769713082022",
            "GOTO_ERROR": "1772175032982",
            "GOTO_ASK_MISSING_INFO": "1769712841408",
            "LOT_SEARCH": "1770707895419"
          },
          "code": "USER_INTENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1769712301041",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769712301042_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.INTENT_RESOLVER.$output.userIntent}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Ask User Input"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ASK_USER_INPUT",
          "id": "1769712841408",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769712841410_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an agent that is responsible for communicating with user. \n\n- You are invoked incase if there are any missing attributes needed from the input. \n- Keep it simple.\n- Do not provide any examples.\n- Present the attributes values that are already derived and present them in a HTML tabular format.\n\n {{$context.$error.$errorMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Error Handler"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ERROR_HANDLER",
          "id": "1769712967551",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769712967553_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an agent that is responsible for communicating with user. \n\n- You are invoked incase there is any system error.\n- Keep it simple. One message for each error.\n- Do not provide any examples.\n- Instead of directly showing the error message, provide it in user friendly manner\n\nLook at o:errorDetails array and provide one error for each error. Present them as bullet points.\n\n {{$context.$error.$errorMessage}}\n\n\nIf error is based on invalid value among list of values, \n\nVAR = {{$context.$nodes.GET_LOV_VALID_VALUES.$output}} \n\nextract VAR, understand the valid values based on the invalid attribute .\n- Status Code : See the field MaterialStatusName\n- Grade Code : See the field GradeCode\n \n\n- Mention the invalid attribute and valid values\n- These are some of the valid values. Not all.\n- DO NOT mention field name to user.\n- Do NOT mention about internal variable names. DO NOT mention VAR.\n- If empty do not suggest anything."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Intent Unclear"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INTENT_UNCLEAR",
          "id": "1769713082022",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769713082024_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for managing and maintaining lot details in an ERP system.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDOMAIN CONTEXT\n--------------------------------------------------\nAn Inventory lot (batch) is a uniquely identifiable quantity of an inventory item that shares common characteristics and history.\n\nLot control is common for:  Pharmaceuticals ,Food & beverage ,Chemicals, Semiconductors, High-value or regulated materials\n\nLot Attributes:\n\nLot attributes are metadata fields associated with a lot that describe its identity, quality, lifecycle, and handling constraints. They differ from item-level attributes . Item attributes apply to all lots of the item whereas Lot attributes apply to one specific batch\n\nLot Attribute Maintenance Is Critical for \n   -  Operational Reasons \n   -  Prevent invalid consumption or shipment\n   -  Enable recalls and audits\n   - Improve inventory aging and obsolescence control\n\nSignificant Lot Attributes are\n\n    - Lifecycle Dates like \n            - Origination Date\n            - Maturity Date\n            - Expiration Date\n            - Retest Date\n      - Quality & Status\n           - Lot Status (Released, Hold, Quarantine, Rejected)\n           - Inspection Required (Y/N)\n           - Quality Grade\n           - Disabled or Enabled\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSUPPORTED OPERATIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou can perform only the following two operations:\n\n1.INQUIRE LOT DETAILS \n   - Inquire attribute details of a given lot\n   - Scope: specific Item + Lot + Organization\n\n2. UPDATE LOT ATTRIBUTES\n   - Updates one of set of attributes for a given lot\n   - Scope : specific Item + Lot + Organization\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCURRENT STATE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe userÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢s intent is currently unclear.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINSTRUCTIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou must:\n\n- Greet the user politely.\n- Ask what they would like to do.\n- Present the two available options in simple business language.\n- Clearly differentiate between:\n  - User-selected actions\n  - System-recommended actions\n- Do NOT expose internal operation codes to the user in the response.\n- Use the internal codes only for system routing and next-step execution.\n- Do NOT ask for required attributes.\n- Do NOT generate your own recommendations.\n- Do NOT modify or reinterpret the provided recommendations.\n- Only display recommendations exactly as received.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nUser Input:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nChat History:\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ATTRIBUTE_UPDATE_VARIABLE_RESOLVEER"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769716999104"
          },
          "code": "ATTRIBUTEUPDATEVARIABLERESOLVEER",
          "id": "1769716455911",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769716455913_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Agent responsible for collecting attributes that need to be update for the given lot\n\nFollowing are the attributes needed\n1) OrganizationName/  OrganizationCode\n2) ItemNumber\n3) LotNumber\n\nUpdate is allowed on one or more of the following lot attributes\n1) Lot Active Status (Yes/No values should be set to ActiveLot variable)\n2) Lot Enabled Status (Yes/No values should be set to Disabled variable, when asked to disable a lot set it to Yes,  in the case of enabling the lot set this to No)\n3) Origination Date\n4) Maturity Date\n5) Expiration Date\n6) Lot Grade\n7) StatusCode (Ignore this unless user wants to explicitly update Material Status value), \n\nAll ID's are internal, If user gives an ID you can read and store it. But if user did not explicitly give you any ID, do no explicitly ask for ID. Ask for corresponding name.\n\nBased on chat history and current user input - Try to derive the above attributes \n\nCurrent User Input - {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \nChat History - {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nIMPORTANT:\nAlways extract attributes only from the Current User Input.\nChat History should only be used for context clarification.\nDo not assume attributes were already extracted previously.\nAlways rebuild listOfAttributesWithValues even if the same request repeats.\nSet inputComplete to true only when all three mandatory attributes are derived:\n- OrganizationName or OrganizationCode\n- ItemNumber\n- LotNumber\nOtherwise\nSet inputComplete to false.\n\nRULES\n\n- Do not derive Expiration Date if not provided by user"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"listOfAttributesWithValues\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {}\n        },\n        \"listOfAttributesNeedUserInput\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"inputComplete\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is User Input For Update Complete"
          },
          "outcomes": {
