          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772184713929_1",
              "name": "pOrganizationId",
              "type": "number",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_ORG_RESOLVER.$output.items?.[0]?.OrganizationId}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1772184713930_2",
              "name": "pItemNumber",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.UPDATEATTRIBUTEREQUESTCREATOR.$output.ItemNumber}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Update Attribute Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "UPDATE_ATTRIBUTE_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1769719798645",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769719798646_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Agent responsible for communicating completion results to the end user.\n\nYou will receive two inputs:\n1) Validation Result: {{$context.$nodes.VALIDATE_INPUT.$output.result}}\n2) Update Response Data: {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_LOT_ATTRIBUTES.$output}}\n\n==================================================\nDECISION RULE (STRICT)\n==================================================\nA) If {{$context.$nodes.VALIDATE_INPUT.$output.result}} == \"SUCCESS\":\n   - Render the SUCCESS output only (see SUCCESS section).\n   - Do NOT render any error text.\n\nB) Else ({{$context.$nodes.VALIDATE_INPUT.$output.result}} != \"SUCCESS\"):\n   - Render the CUSTOM ERRORS output only (see CUSTOM ERRORS section).\n   - Do NOT render any success tables or success confirmation message.\n   - Output MUST be exactly one user-facing error message mapped from the validation result:\n     - If the value matches a known error key in \"Error mapping\", use its user-facing message.\n     - If the value does NOT match any known error key, output the following generic message exactly:\n       \"We couldnÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â€žÂ¢t update the lot attributes due to an input validation error. Please review your entries and try again.\"\n\n==================================================\nSUCCESS\n==================================================\nInput Data:\n{{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_LOT_ATTRIBUTES.$output}}\n\nCOMMON ATTRIBUTE MAPPING (Input Record Object -> Display Attribute)\n- Lot Number:        LotNumber\n- Organization Name: OrganizationName\n- Item Number:       ItemNumber\n- Item Description:  ItemDescription\n- Lot Status:        LotStatusMeaning   (apply STATUS DISPLAY RULE)\n- Active Lot:        ActiveLot\n- Material Status:   StatusCode\n- Maturity Date:     MaturityDate       (apply DATE DISPLAY RULE: date only)\n- Hold Until Date:   HoldUntilDate      (apply DATE DISPLAY RULE: date only)\n- Origination Date:  OriginationDate    (apply DATE DISPLAY RULE: date only)\n- Expiration Date:   ExpirationDate     (apply DATE DISPLAY RULE: date only)\n- Grade:             GradeDescription\n\nYour responsibilities:\n1. Interpret the input data and identify only records that were successfully updated.\n   - If the input contains multiple records, include ONLY the successful ones.\n   - If no records are successful, render no tables and still render the confirmation message ONLY if the overall operation is clearly successful; otherwise render nothing beyond what is explicitly supported by the data.\n2. Do not display or mention any:\n   - internal system codes\n   - internal identifiers\n   - technical reference IDs\n3. For each successful updated record, present results as an HTML vertical table (attribute-value layout) with NO borders:\n   - Use <table> (no border attribute)\n   - Each row must be: <tr><td><b>Attribute</b></td><td>Value</td></tr>\n   - Column 1 labels must be bold using <b>...</b>\n   - Attribute in column 1\n   - Value in column 2\n4. For each record, display ONLY the following attributes in this exact order:\n   - Lot Number\n   - Organization Name\n   - Item Number\n   - Item Description\n   - Lot Status\n   - Active Lot\n   - Material Status\n   - Maturity Date\n   - Hold Until Date\n   - Origination Date\n   - Expiration Date\n   - Grade\n5. If there are multiple successful records:\n   - Render one vertical table per record\n   - Separate records with <hr>\n\nSTATUS DISPLAY RULE:\n If Lot Status (DisabledCode) = \"Y\" display exactly: Disabled\n- If Lot Status (DisabledCode) is anything else  display: Enabled\n\nDATE DISPLAY RULE:\n- All date/datetime fields must be displayed as Date only (no time part).\n\nNULL DISPLAY RULE:\n- If a field is null/undefined/unavailable, display as blank.\n\nAfter the record table(s), display exactly this confirmation message:\nÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã…â€œThe lot  attributes have been successfully updated using the new values.ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¯Â¿Â½\n\nOutput Rules (Success):\n- Output must be HTML only.\n- Do not include explanations, system messages, or backend details.\n- Do not expose raw payloads or JSON.\n- Ensure the tone is clear, professional, and user-friendly.\n\n==================================================\nCUSTOM ERRORS\n==================================================\nIf no successful records exist:\nDisplay the message:\n\"No lot attributes were updated.\"\nBased on {{$context.$nodes.VALIDATE_INPUT.$output.result}} explain error to user\n\nInstructions:\n- Output MUST be HTML only.\n- Output MUST contain ONLY the mapped user-facing message text (no extra sentences, no headers, no bullets).\n- Do NOT include any comments, explanations, actions, or backend details.\n\nError mapping (validation result -> user-facing message):\n- ERROR_EXPIRATION_DATE_SYS_DEFINED\n  \"You are not allowed to update Expiration Date for this lot because the item has system-defined expiration date control.\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query Onhand Creator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770707929754"
          },
          "code": "QUERY_ONHAND_CREATOR",
          "id": "1770707895419",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770707895421_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for generating the **q query parameter** for an ADF REST API that searches inventory lot records.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUSER INPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\nInputs:\n- Current User Input:\n  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Chat History:\n  {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\nProduce a response that:\n1) Generates a valid ADF REST `q` parameter\n2) Includes Organization and Item filters directly in the query when provided\n3) Treats ALL attributes as optional\n4) Always conforms to the required output schema\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT VARIABLES\n--------------------------------------------------\nThe agent may receive the following inputs:\n\n1) Free-text search text\n2) Explicit parameters such as:\n   - Organization Name\n   - Organization Code\n   - OrganizationId\n   - Item Number\n   - InventoryItemId\n   - LotNumber\n   - Status\n   - Grade\n   - Dates\n   - Other lot attributes\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMANDATORY INPUT RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\nThere are NO mandatory parameters.\n\n- All attributes are optional.\n- If no valid filters are identified, return an empty query string.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUERY GENERATION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1) Include filters ONLY when explicitly mentioned or clearly implied.\n2) Never invent values.\n3) Never auto-correct values.\n4) Never infer missing Organization or Item values.\n5) Combine all conditions using logical AND.\n6) Use proper ADF REST `q` syntax.\n7) Properly quote string fields using single quotes only.\n8) Preserve exact user-entered values.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUOTING RULE (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- All string values MUST be enclosed in single quotes (' ').\n- NEVER use double quotes (\") in the query.\n- Do NOT escape using backslashes.\n- Numeric values must NOT be quoted.\n- Date values must be enclosed in single quotes.\n- Boolean values must NOT be quoted unless provided as literal strings by the user.\n- Preserve exact user-entered values inside single quotes.\n\nCorrect:\nOrganizationCode='PDSCV1'\nItemNumber='500 GB Internal Memory'\nLotNumber='LIM100'\n\nIncorrect:\nOrganizationCode=\"PDSCV1\"\nOrganizationCode=\\\"PDSCV1\\\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSUPPORTED FILTERABLE ATTRIBUTES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOrganization-level:\n- OrganizationId\n- OrganizationCode\n- OrganizationName\n\nItem-level:\n- InventoryItemId\n- ItemNumber\n\nLot-level:\n- LotNumber\n- ParentLotNumber\n- ActiveLot\n- ActiveLotCode\n- StatusCode\n- Grade\n- OriginationType\n- ExpirationDate\n- OriginationDate\n- MaturityDate\n- ExpirationActionCode\n- ExpirationAction\n- ExpirationActionDate\n- HoldUntilDate\n- RetestDate\n- Disabled\n- DualUOMFlag\n- UniqueDeviceIdentifier\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBASE CONDITION\n--------------------------------------------------\nThere is NO mandatory base condition.\nDo NOT inject default filters such as ActiveLot='Yes' unless explicitly requested.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUERY CONSTRUCTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Join multiple filters using AND.\n- If only one filter exists, return it directly.\n- If no valid filters exist, return an empty string.\n- Do NOT wrap the entire query in quotes.\n- Return only the condition expression (not prefixed with q"
            }
          ],
